From eb14ba72596529b269864c471bf506d14cae6629 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:03:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): a relay names only a message a person typed; the
 card holder refuses replayed and pre-ask relays [daveey]

Review 5878485674 on #1583 (kanban-d1b921f32e):

1. verify() took the session's newest role='user' row, so a synthetic row (above all the card's own
   needs_input kanban_notice, which always lands after the ask) could "verify" a relay with no reply from
   David and bring back the ping-pong the no-progress budget stops. _latest_user_message now picks the
   newest row a person typed: display_kind NULL/'' or 'steer', not a compaction summary, not a
   "[System:" notice or a session-mentions cross-session delivery.
2. A cross-gateway relay was stored after a shape check only: replays and pre-ask messages counted.
   New kanban_relayed_human.admit(), called by add_comment inside its write transaction (atomic) and by
   the dashboard endpoint first (HTTP 400): the card asked, the message is not older than its latest ask
   (REMOTE_CLOCK_SKEW_SECONDS=120 for a remote origin), and no (session, message_id) is relayed twice.
